### Ready-made requests for the IntelliJ HTTP Client (or VS Code REST Client).
### The service trusts X-Forwarded-For from localhost, so it stands in for the client IP.
### 212.77.98.9 is in Poland (wp.pl), 46.4.0.1 in Germany (Hetzner), according to the DB-IP database.

### Create a coupon (the code is case-insensitive and stored upper case)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "wiosna", "maxUses": 2, "country": "PL"}

### A coupon valid through December only (validUntil is exclusive); redeeming it earlier gives 409 COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "zima", "maxUses": 100, "country": "PL", "validFrom": "2026-12-01T00:00:00Z", "validUntil": "2027-01-01T00:00:00Z"}

### Read it back, in any case
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/Wiosna

### Redeem from Poland: 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/WIOSNA/redemptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 212.77.98.9

{"userId": "user-1"}

### Same user again: 409 COUPON_ALREADY_REDEEMED
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/WIOSNA/redemptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 212.77.98.9

{"userId": "user-1"}

### Did user-1's redemption go through? 200 (404 REDEMPTION_NOT_FOUND for a user who has not redeemed it)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/WIOSNA/redemptions/user-1

### From Germany: 403 COUPON_COUNTRY_NOT_ALLOWED
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/WIOSNA/redemptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 46.4.0.1

{"userId": "user-2"}

### Unknown coupon: 404 COUPON_NOT_FOUND
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/NIE-MA/redemptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 212.77.98.9

{"userId": "user-1"}

### Metrics by outcome
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/prometheus
